From 31973106108dc0e2689d3bdb05b03938fd57fed3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ole Algoritme <olealgoritme@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 14:17:36 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] nak: uniform 64-bit address bases in divergent ifs stay in
 pinned UGPRs (NAK_UADDR_PIN)

In uniform control flow, nak_nir_opt_uniform_address moves the uniform
part of a global memory address into the access's UGPR address: LDG
[Rx.U32 + URy] or [RZ + URy].  In divergent control flow it could not,
since NAK cannot write UGPRs there and the legalizer copies uniform
vectors that are not pinned to GPRs.  vkd3d-proton shaders do most of
their work under a divergent branch, so every descriptor heap or root
constant buffer access there computed its address in GPRs (MOV R, UR;
IADD3; IADD3.X) or reloaded it from the constant buffer (two LDCs) just
before the load.  In the six heaviest Steel Nomad fragment shaders that
was about 30% of NAK's extra instructions over the reference compiler.

For each top-level divergent if, nak_nir_pin_uniform_addresses takes the
uniform 64-bit bases of the global loads, stores and atomics inside it
that can be computed before it (ALU, constant buffer loads, immediates),
computes them in the block before the if, where they are in UGPRs, and
pins them for the region as nak_nir_lower_non_uniform_ldcx does for
bindless cbuf handles: at most 4 pairs per region and 8 pinned pairs in
total.  The access then takes the base as its uniform address and at
most a zero-extended 32-bit GPR offset.  Divergent loops are left alone:
there the different spill costs make the occupancy target keep 8 warps
instead of 12 on the two big compute shaders.

The rematerializer learns the new form: a load through a pinned pair
whose live range covers the value's is rematerializable, and a pinned
pair loaded from a bound constant buffer uses the shader-wide pinned
address of NAK_OCC_TARGET, so the occupancy target keeps choosing the
same register counts.

Offline, GB202, Steel Nomad (NAK_UADDR_PIN=0 -> 1): fragment 143389 ->
137542 instructions, static cycles -6.6%; compute 70416 -> 69131; no
shader loses occupancy, several gain it; seven fragment shaders get 2
memory spills and 1 fill, none in a loop.  CS2 compute -9.2%.
